<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Aug vs Aug industrial output by sector.</title>
<headline>Argentine Aug vs Aug industrial output by sector.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a sectorial breakdown of growth in Argentine industrial output in August compared to the same period in 1995:</p>
<p>    Detergents and soap:		  36.6</p>
<p>    Plastic manufactures:		 33.2</p>
<p>    Cars:				     28.6</p>
<p>    Textiles:				 26.7</p>
<p>    Flour:				    24.6</p>
<p>    Synthetic fibers:		     24.2</p>
<p>    Beer:				     24.1</p>
<p>    Bread and pasta:			23.8</p>
<p>    Lampblack:				22.0</p>
<p>    Tires:				    21.6</p>
<p>    Agricultural chemicals:	     19.4</p>
<p>    Primary iron:			   18.4</p>
<p>    Cotton thread:			  15.9</p>
<p>    Raw steel:				12.4</p>
<p>    Assorted construction materials:   6.9</p>
<p>    Basic chemical products:	     6.8</p>
<p>    Refined petroleum:		     6.6</p>
<p>    Vegetable oils			   5.7</p>
<p>    Plastics and synthetic resins:     5.6</p>
<p>    Hot laminates:			   4.0</p>
<p>    Dairy products			   3.8</p>
<p>    Liquor:				    1.9</p>
<p>    Primary aluminum:			1.0</p>
<p>    Paper:				     0.2</p>
<p>    Car parts:				 0.1</p>
<p>    Soft drinks:			    -0.1</p>
<p>    Industrial gases:		     -0.2</p>
<p>    Cement:				   -1.2</p>
<p>    Cigarettes:			     -1.6</p>
<p>    Red meat:				 -5.7</p>
<p>    Pharmaceutical products:	    -5.9</p>
<p>    Cold laminates:			 -6.2</p>
<p>    Mate tea:				 -9.4</p>
<p>    White meat:			    -11.3</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655</p>
